Bugfix: Reject unknown users as slowly as wrong passwords

Rest-server rejected a username that does not exist in the `.htpasswd` file
much faster than a wrong password for an existing user. The response time
allowed an attacker to find out which usernames exist, which also reveals the
repository names when using `--private-repos`.

Unknown usernames and wrong passwords are now rejected in the same amount of
time.

https://github.com/restic/rest-server/pull/416
